### Chat Service API Documentation
### Complete API documentation for chat service proxy endpoints

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000/api/chat
@contentType = application/json
@token = your-jwt-token-here
@internalSecret = your-internal-secret-here

### ============================================
### HEALTH CHECK
### ============================================
### Check chat service health status
### No authentication required

GET {{baseUrl}}/health
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

### Response Example:
### {
###   "status": "ok",
###   "timestamp": "2024-01-01T00:00:00.000Z"
### }

### ============================================
### USERS - SYNC (INTERNAL)
### ============================================
### Sync a single user profile to the chat service
### Internal endpoint - uses X-Internal-Secret header
### Called automatically by backend on user create/update

POST {{baseUrl}}/users/sync
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
X-Internal-Secret: {{internalSecret}}

{
  "externalUserId": "user_123",
  "displayName": "Jane Doe",
  "avatarUrl": "https://example.com/avatar.png",
  "metadata": {
    "phone": "+1234567890",
    "mode": "freelancer",
    "country": "US"
  }
}

### Response: 200 OK

### ============================================
### USERS - BATCH SYNC (INTERNAL)
### ============================================
### Sync multiple users in a single request
### Internal endpoint - uses X-Internal-Secret header
### More efficient for bulk operations

POST {{baseUrl}}/users/sync/batch
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
X-Internal-Secret: {{internalSecret}}

{
  "users": [
    {
      "externalUserId": "user_1",
      "displayName": "User One",
      "avatarUrl": "https://example.com/avatar1.png",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "externalUserId": "user_2",
      "displayName": "User Two",
      "avatarUrl": null,
      "metadata": {}
    }
  ]
}

### Response: 200 OK
### Note: Use npm run chat:sync for bulk operations

### ============================================
### GET USER FROM CHAT SERVICE
### ============================================
### Get user information from chat service
### Requires JWT Bearer token

GET {{baseUrl}}/users/:externalUserId
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Replace :externalUserId with actual user ID
### Example: GET {{baseUrl}}/users/user_123

### ============================================
### DELETE USER FROM CHAT SERVICE
### ============================================
### Delete a user from the chat service
### Requires JWT Bearer token

DELETE {{baseUrl}}/users/:externalUserId
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Replace :externalUserId with actual user ID
### Example: DELETE {{baseUrl}}/users/user_123

### ============================================
### CREATE CONVERSATION
### ============================================
### Create a new conversation (direct or group)
### Requires JWT Bearer token

POST {{baseUrl}}/conversations
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "type": "direct",
  "participantIds": ["user_1", "user_2"]
}

### Request Body Fields:
### - type: "direct" or "group" (required)
### - participantIds: Array of user IDs (required, min 2 for direct)

### Response Example (201 Created):
### {
###   "id": "conv_123",
###   "type": "direct",
###   "participants": [...],
###   "createdAt": "2024-01-01T00:00:00.000Z"
### }

### ============================================
### GET CONVERSATIONS
### ============================================
### List conversations for the authenticated user
### Requires JWT Bearer token

GET {{baseUrl}}/conversations?limit=20&type=direct&cursor=
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Query Parameters:
### - limit: Number of results to return (optional, number)
### - cursor: Pagination cursor (optional, string)
### - type: Filter by conversation type - "direct" or "group" (optional)

### ============================================
### GET CONVERSATION BY ID
### ============================================
### Get conversation details
### Requires JWT Bearer token

GET {{baseUrl}}/conversations/:id
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Replace :id with actual conversation ID
### Example: GET {{baseUrl}}/conversations/conv_123

### ============================================
### DELETE/LEAVE CONVERSATION
### ============================================
### Delete or leave a conversation
### Requires JWT Bearer token

DELETE {{baseUrl}}/conversations/:id?mode=leave
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Replace :id with actual conversation ID
### Query Parameters:
### - mode: "leave" or "delete" (optional, default: "leave")

### ============================================
### ADD PARTICIPANT TO CONVERSATION
### ============================================
### Add a participant to a conversation
### Requires JWT Bearer token

POST {{baseUrl}}/conversations/:id/participants
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "externalUserId": "user_3",
  "role": "member"
}

### Replace :id with actual conversation ID
### Request Body Fields:
### - externalUserId: User ID to add (required, string)
### - role: Participant role (optional, string, e.g., "member", "admin")

### ============================================
### UPDATE PARTICIPANT ROLE
### ============================================
### Update a participant's role in a conversation
### Requires JWT Bearer token

PATCH {{baseUrl}}/conversations/:id/participants/:userId
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "role": "admin"
}

### Replace :id with conversation ID and :userId with user ID
### Request Body Fields:
### - role: New role for participant (required, string)

### ============================================
### REMOVE PARTICIPANT FROM CONVERSATION
### ============================================
### Remove a participant from a conversation
### Requires JWT Bearer token

DELETE {{baseUrl}}/conversations/:id/participants/:userId
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Replace :id with conversation ID and :userId with user ID

### ============================================
### SEND MESSAGE
### ============================================
### Send a message in a conversation
### Requires JWT Bearer token

POST {{baseUrl}}/conversations/:conversationId/messages
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "content": "Hello, how are you?",
  "attachments": [
    {
      "externalFileId": "file_123",
      "type": "image",
      "url": "https://example.com/file.jpg"
    }
  ]
}

### Replace :conversationId with actual conversation ID
### Request Body Fields:
### - content: Message text content (required, string)
### - attachments: Array of attachment objects (optional)

### Attachment Object:
### {
###   "externalFileId": "file_123",
###   "type": "image" | "file" | "video" | etc.,
###   "url": "https://example.com/file.jpg"
### }

### ============================================
### GET MESSAGES FROM CONVERSATION
### ============================================
### Get messages from a conversation
### Requires JWT Bearer token

GET {{baseUrl}}/conversations/:conversationId/messages?limit=50&after=msg_456&before=&includeDeleted=false
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Replace :conversationId with actual conversation ID
### Query Parameters:
### - limit: Number of messages to return (optional, number)
### - before: Get messages before this message ID (optional, string)
### - after: Get messages after this message ID (optional, string)
### - includeDeleted: Include deleted messages (optional, boolean, default: false)

### ============================================
### GET MESSAGE BY ID
### ============================================
### Get a specific message by ID
### Requires JWT Bearer token

GET {{baseUrl}}/messages/:id
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Replace :id with actual message ID
### Example: GET {{baseUrl}}/messages/msg_123

### ============================================
### EDIT MESSAGE
### ============================================
### Edit a message
### Requires JWT Bearer token

PATCH {{baseUrl}}/messages/:id
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "content": "Edited message content"
}

### Replace :id with actual message ID
### Request Body Fields:
### - content: Updated message content (required, string)

### ============================================
### DELETE MESSAGE
### ============================================
### Delete a message
### Requires JWT Bearer token

DELETE {{baseUrl}}/messages/:id
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Replace :id with actual message ID
### Example: DELETE {{baseUrl}}/messages/msg_123

### ============================================
### ADD REACTION TO MESSAGE
### ============================================
### Add a reaction to a message
### Requires JWT Bearer token

POST {{baseUrl}}/messages/:messageId/reactions
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "emoji": "👍"
}

### Replace :messageId with actual message ID
### Request Body Fields:
### - emoji: Emoji to add as reaction (required, string)

### ============================================
### REMOVE REACTION FROM MESSAGE
### ============================================
### Remove a reaction from a message
### Requires JWT Bearer token

DELETE {{baseUrl}}/messages/:messageId/reactions/:emoji
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Replace :messageId with message ID and :emoji with emoji to remove
### Note: Emoji should be URL encoded
### Example: DELETE {{baseUrl}}/messages/msg_123/reactions/%F0%9F%91%8D

### ============================================
### GET MESSAGE REACTIONS
### ============================================
### Get all reactions for a message
### Requires JWT Bearer token

GET {{baseUrl}}/messages/:messageId/reactions
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Replace :messageId with actual message ID
### Example: GET {{baseUrl}}/messages/msg_123/reactions

### ============================================
### MARK MESSAGE AS READ
### ============================================
### Mark a message as read
### Requires JWT Bearer token

PUT {{baseUrl}}/messages/:messageId/read
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Replace :messageId with actual message ID
### No request body required
### Example: PUT {{baseUrl}}/messages/msg_123/read

### ============================================
### MARK CONVERSATION AS READ
### ============================================
### Mark all messages up to a certain point as read in a conversation
### Requires JWT Bearer token

PUT {{baseUrl}}/conversations/:conversationId/read
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "upToMessageId": "msg_456"
}

### Replace :conversationId with actual conversation ID
### Request Body Fields:
### - upToMessageId: Message ID to mark as read up to (optional, string)

### ============================================
### GET MESSAGE READ RECEIPTS
### ============================================
### Get read receipt information for a message
### Requires JWT Bearer token

GET {{baseUrl}}/messages/:messageId/read
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Replace :messageId with actual message ID
### Example: GET {{baseUrl}}/messages/msg_123/read

### ============================================
### GET UNREAD COUNT
### ============================================
### Get unread message count for a conversation
### Requires JWT Bearer token

GET {{baseUrl}}/conversations/:conversationId/unread-count
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Replace :conversationId with actual conversation ID
### Example: GET {{baseUrl}}/conversations/conv_123/unread-count

### ============================================
### GET USER PRESENCE
### ============================================
### Get user presence status
### Requires JWT Bearer token

GET {{baseUrl}}/users/:userId/presence
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Replace :userId with actual user ID
### Example: GET {{baseUrl}}/users/user_123/presence

### ============================================
### GET CONVERSATION PRESENCE
### ============================================
### Get presence status for all participants in a conversation
### Requires JWT Bearer token

GET {{baseUrl}}/conversations/:conversationId/presence
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Replace :conversationId with actual conversation ID
### Example: GET {{baseUrl}}/conversations/conv_123/presence

### ============================================
### GET BATCH PRESENCE
### ============================================
### Get presence status for multiple users
### Requires JWT Bearer token

POST {{baseUrl}}/presence/batch
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "userIds": ["user_1", "user_2", "user_3"]
}

### Request Body Fields:
### - userIds: Array of user IDs to get presence for (required, array of strings)

### ============================================
### COMPREHENSIVE NOTES & GUIDELINES
### ============================================

### 1. AUTHENTICATION & AUTHORIZATION
###    - Public endpoints (no auth required):
###      * GET /api/chat/health (health check)
###    - User endpoints (requires JWT Bearer token):
###      * All other endpoints require Authorization: Bearer <token>
###    - Internal endpoints (uses X-Internal-Secret header):
###      * POST /api/chat/users/sync (sync single user)
###      * POST /api/chat/users/sync/batch (sync multiple users)

### 2. BASE URL
###    - Development: http://localhost:5000/api/chat
###    - Production: https://api.example.com/api/chat

### 3. ERROR RESPONSES
###    - 400 Bad Request: Invalid request data or parameters
###    - 401 Unauthorized: Missing or invalid JWT token
###    - 403 Forbidden: Insufficient permissions or invalid internal secret
###    - 404 Not Found: Resource not found
###    - 500 Internal Server Error: Server error
###    - 503 Service Unavailable: Chat service unavailable

### Example Error Response:
### {
###   "statusCode": 400,
###   "message": "Validation failed",
###   "error": "Bad Request",
###   "details": {
###     "field": "participantIds",
###     "message": "At least 2 participants required for direct conversation"
###   }
### }

### 4. CONVERSATION TYPES
###    - "direct": One-on-one conversation between two users
###    - "group": Group conversation with multiple participants

### 5. MESSAGE ATTACHMENTS
###    - Attachments can include files, images, videos, etc.
###    - Each attachment requires:
###      * externalFileId: Reference to file in external system
###      * type: Type of attachment (image, file, video, etc.)
###      * url: URL to access the file

### 6. REACTIONS
###    - Reactions are emoji-based
###    - Multiple users can react with the same emoji
###    - Emoji should be URL encoded when used in DELETE requests

### 7. READ RECEIPTS
###    - Messages can be marked as read individually
###    - Conversations can be marked as read up to a specific message
###    - Read receipts track which users have read which messages

### 8. PRESENCE
###    - Presence indicates user online/offline status
###    - Can be checked for individual users or all participants in a conversation
###    - Batch presence check available for multiple users

### 9. PAGINATION
###    - Conversations and messages support cursor-based pagination
###    - Use "cursor" parameter for conversations
###    - Use "before" and "after" parameters for messages
###    - "limit" parameter controls number of results

### 10. USER SYNC
###     - Users are automatically synced when created or updated
###     - Manual sync available via npm run chat:sync
###     - Batch sync more efficient for bulk operations

### 11. WEBSOCKET CONNECTION
###     - For real-time messaging, connect directly to chat service WebSocket
###     - Use JWT token in Socket.IO handshake:
###       const socket = io('ws://chat.example.com', {
###         auth: {
###           token: 'your-jwt-token'
###         }
###       });

### 12. CONFIGURATION
###     - Ensure .env file has:
###       CHAT_SERVICE_URL=http://localhost:3000
###       CHAT_INTERNAL_API_SECRET=your-secret-here
###       CHAT_SERVICE_ENABLED=true
###     - CHAT_INTERNAL_API_SECRET must match chat service's INTERNAL_API_SECRET

### 13. USAGE EXAMPLES

### Example 1: Create Direct Conversation
POST {{baseUrl}}/conversations
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "type": "direct",
  "participantIds": ["user_1", "user_2"]
}

### Example 2: Send Message with Attachment
POST {{baseUrl}}/conversations/conv_123/messages
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "content": "Check out this image!",
  "attachments": [
    {
      "externalFileId": "file_123",
      "type": "image",
      "url": "https://example.com/image.jpg"
    }
  ]
}

### Example 3: Get Messages with Pagination
GET {{baseUrl}}/conversations/conv_123/messages?limit=50&after=msg_456
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Example 4: Add Reaction
POST {{baseUrl}}/messages/msg_123/reactions
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "emoji": "❤️"
}

### Example 5: Mark Conversation as Read
PUT {{baseUrl}}/conversations/conv_123/read
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "upToMessageId": "msg_789"
}

### Example 6: Check Multiple Users Presence
POST {{baseUrl}}/presence/batch
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "userIds": ["user_1", "user_2", "user_3"]
}

### 14. BEST PRACTICES
###     - Always include Authorization header for protected endpoints
###     - Use pagination for large result sets
###     - Handle errors appropriately
###     - Use WebSocket for real-time features
###     - Cache presence data appropriately
###     - Implement proper retry logic for failed requests

### 15. RATE LIMITING
###     - Rate limiting is handled by the chat service
###     - Proxy forwards all requests to chat service
###     - Check chat service documentation for rate limits
